{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790277798,"nonce":"P7cOSYNaUyx6d8EETgazbMjqFNE=","title":"deltablue iteration 1: functions with loops still compile through the per-function pipeline on the caller's thread","message":"With quick baselines for loop-free functions (a stub's first call compiles the interpreter's body at tier 0 and the worker replaces it), deltablue -n 5 iteration 1 on the NUC went from about 130 ms to about 92 ms (median of 10 interleaved runs against the 8844ca79 binary), not the 10 to 20 ms planned. The plan assumed most of the 54 stub compiles were loop-free methods. In a traced run 68 functions take quick baselines (about 1 ms each on the loaded NUC, 0.4 to 0.6 ms on the Mac), but 12 functions with loops still take the whole pipeline on zyntax-first-call-compile while the main thread waits:\n\n    chain_test, projection_test, change, change$trusted, Plan$execute,\n    Planner$incremental_add, Planner$incremental_remove$trusted,\n    Planner$add_propagate$trusted, Planner$add_constraints_consuming_to,\n    Planner$extract_plan_from_constraints, Planner$make_plan,\n    Planner$remove_propagate_from\n\nTheir pipeline time is 60 ms on the Mac and about 160 ms traced on the NUC (projection_test 34 ms body, remove_propagate_from 20 ms, change 22 ms). Iteration 1 is still about 100x iteration 5 (0.8 ms), so the 8x target in the brief is not met.\n\nA frame of a function with a loop cannot run a quick baseline: its resume points are made for the optimised body (keyed by body_tag), and a long-running frame would stay in unoptimised code for the whole call (the reverted nbody experiment). Options: an outlined region per loop for a stub-called function, as the interpreter already gets (publish_outlined_resume_point), so the quick code of a function with loops leaves each loop through a region optimised on its own; or cutting the pipeline's per-function cost for these bodies (see 5200715 on the inliner's share).\n\nReproduce: ZYPY_LLVM=1 ZYNTAX_TRACE_LAZY=1 zypy run deltablue.py -n 5 in a directory staged as benchmarks/speed/run.py stages it; the lines ending \"loops) on zyntax-first-call-compile\" are these compiles.","files":null}]}